From 94e33cf7c559da040cf486cd99d1cc77b42e8786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:54:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(trace): gate the trace at run time and time the
 window path

Local (Asahi/Honeykrisp) latency tooling.

- REIMS_VGPU_TRACE_GATE names a file: with REIMS_VGPU_TRACE set, events
  are written only while it exists (looked at every 200 ms), so a
  long-running VM keeps the variable and traces a window of interest.
- REIMS_VGPU_TUNE names a key=value file read at run time
  (trace::tune); the window's swapchain takes `present_mode`
  (mailbox, fifo, immediate, fifo_relaxed) from it where the surface
  offers it, and is made again in that mode.
- Window events: wnew (the guest presented), wdraw (the render thread
  takes the draw), wacq (image taken, fence waited), wsched (frame
  scheduled), wpres (vkQueuePresentKHR returned). The offered present
  modes are logged at info.
